            <div xml:id="d185">

                <pb facs="0358" n="244" sameAs="frus:frus1924v01/pg244"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.2300/68: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Kellogg</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-03-06T18:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 6, 1924—6
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received March 6—2:42
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>87. My telegram no. 61, February 15, 4 p.m., <hi rendition="#italic">re</hi>
                    world aeroplane flight. The British Government agrees to waive usual
                    restrictions on aerial photography in the case of the five aeroplanes, provided
                    they do not fly over or photograph any of prohibited areas named in schedule 7
                    of Air Navigation Order 1923, copy of which I am forwarding you,<anchor n="24"
                        xml:id="d185-f1"/> or the areas in which armament depots are situated at
                    Woolwich, Bedenham, Marchwood, Bandeath and Wrabness.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
